## The physical system (project-wide invariants)
Facts true across every campaign. No campaign may silently contradict them.
{{SYSTEM_INVARIANTS}}
Everything we know about the system — the full physics, the conventions, the instrument, and the
durable decisions — is `PROJECT_ORIENTATION.md`, beside this file.

## Canonical data — referenced, never copied
- **Location:** {{DATA_LOCATION}} — a read-only `data/` copy, or the resolved `data_path` pointer below.
- **`data_path` (if off-tree):** {{DATA_PATH}}
- **Rule:** campaigns reference the data by relative path (`../../data`). The loop never writes into `data/`
  and never copies it into a campaign. This keeps the tree portable and free of duplicates.

## Shared, promoted artifacts
`shared/` also holds artifacts a campaign froze for siblings to consume, such as a validated forward model or
a generated training set. Each is versioned. Downstream campaigns reference `../../shared/<artifact>`,
never a sibling's working folder. Current promoted artifacts: {{PROMOTED_ARTIFACTS}}

## Layout
`PROJECT.md` (this — what we are trying to achieve) · `PROJECT_ORIENTATION.md` (what we know about
the system, durable decisions included) · `LINEAGE.md` (what has been done) · `DISCOVERIES.md`
(promoted verified findings) · `CLAUDE.md` (always-on rules) · `data/` · `shared/` (promoted frozen
artifacts) · `campaigns/<name>/` · `sessions/<date>_<slug>/` · `reports/`. All internal references
are relative, so the whole tree relocates as one unit.
